[v8 152.2.0] init_stack_vars
[v8 152.2.0]     Current value (from the default) = true
[v8 152.2.0]       From //build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn:144
[v8 152.2.0] 
[v8 152.2.0]     Initialize all local variables with a pattern. This flag will fill
[v8 152.2.0]     uninitialized floating-point types (and 32-bit pointers) with 0xFF and the
[v8 152.2.0]     rest with 0xAA. This makes behavior of uninitialized memory bugs consistent,
[v8 152.2.0]     recognizable in the debugger, and crashes on memory accesses through
[v8 152.2.0]     uninitialized pointers.
[v8 152.2.0]    
[v8 152.2.0]     Flag discussion: https://crbug.com/977230
[v8 152.2.0]    
[v8 152.2.0]     TODO(crbug.com/40721698): This regresses binary size by ~1MB on Android and
[v8 152.2.0]     needs to be evaluated before enabling it there as well.
[v8 152.2.0] 
[v8 152.2.0] init_stack_vars_zero
[v8 152.2.0]     Current value (from the default) = false
[v8 152.2.0]       From //build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn:153
[v8 152.2.0] 
[v8 152.2.0]     Specialization of `init_stack_vars` where locals are initialized with
[v8 152.2.0]     zeroes instead of patterns. Zero init is generally faster and can lead to
[v8 152.2.0]     better binary size due to being able to use instructions taking
[v8 152.2.0]     immediates. Patterns potentially have better signaling behavior though. We
[v8 152.2.0]     thus enable zero-init for all official builds that don't also enable
[v8 152.2.0]     DCHECKs explicitly or implicitly. Note that this intentionally also keeps
[v8 152.2.0]     the patterns for DCHECK Canary releases.
