[v8 152.2.0]     Sets -DV8_ENABLE_PRIVATE_MAPPING_FORK_OPTIMIZATION.
[v8 152.2.0]    
[v8 152.2.0]     This flag speeds up the performance of fork/execve on Linux systems for
[v8 152.2.0]     embedders which use it (like Node.js). It works by marking the pages that
[v8 152.2.0]     V8 allocates as MADV_DONTFORK. Without MADV_DONTFORK, the Linux kernel
[v8 152.2.0]     spends a long time manipulating page mappings on fork and exec which the
[v8 152.2.0]     child process doesn't generally need to access.
[v8 152.2.0]    
[v8 152.2.0]     See v8:7381 for more details.
